1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,620
You can move a thousand times

2
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:03,220
faster than everyone else.

3
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:04,100
To you,

4
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:05,760
the world almost stops.

5
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:07,880
But unlike frozen time,

6
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,580
light still reaches you.

7
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:10,580
You can see.

8
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:12,500
Then you take a step.

9
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:13,740
Walking speed,

10
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:14,780
times a thousand,

11
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:17,120
is five thousand kilometres an hour.

12
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,220
Four times the speed of sound.

13
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:21,040
The air hits you like a

14
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:21,280
wall.

15
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:23,280
Your skin heats up hotter than

16
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:23,780
an oven.

17
00:00:24,280 --> 00:00:26,080
Every step makes a sonic boom

18
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,340
that shatters windows.

19
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:29,340
You could even sprint across a

20
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:30,820
lake without sinking.

21
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:32,460
But you're starving.

22
00:00:33,020 --> 00:00:34,920
Just speeding up burns about sixteen

23
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:36,120
thousand calories.

24
00:00:36,460 --> 00:00:37,940
That's eight days of food,

25
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:39,360
every time you start running.

26
00:00:39,620 --> 00:00:40,580
And it gets worse.

27
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:43,040
One day for everyone else lasts

28
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:44,880
almost three years for you.

29
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:46,740
Your friend blinks...

30
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:47,740
and you've grown old.

31
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:48,540
So,

32
00:00:49,080 --> 00:00:50,540
would you still want super speed?

